  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNFPA PooledFund Co-hosting Global Youth Dialogues in light of ICPD+30 Review</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNFPA organises a review of the ICPD Programme of Action (PoA) every five years. In 2024, this will take place 30 years after the adoption of the PoA. Under ICPD +30, three &quot;Global Dialogues&quot; will be organised. 

These dialogues aim to bring together 200 different stakeholders to celebrate 30 years of ICPD achievements, but also to discuss complex polarising issues and position the ICPD agenda in the sustainable development agenda. Insights and recommendations from the three dialogues will contribute to the global ICPD review report. This report will serve as a basis for deployment in NY, linking the recommendations to the CPD and Summit of the Future. This is crucial given the growing pushback on SRHR &amp; ICPD agenda.

The first dialogue is the youth dialogue and will be co-hosted by NL and Denmark and will take place on 3 and 4 April in Benin. By contributing to the pooled fund, NL contributes to the Global Youth Dialogue in Benin.</narrative>
  </description>
